{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0ADF", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{U}' = \\{X'_i \\to X'\\}_{i \\in I'}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{U} = \\{X_j \\to X\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\alpha : I' \\to I$", "MATH_0005": "$g : X' \\to X$", "MATH_0006": "$g_i : X'_i \\to X_{\\alpha(i)}$", "MATH_0007": "$(V_i, \\varphi_{ij})$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0009": "$$\n\\left(\ng_i^*V_{\\alpha(i)}, (g_i \\times g_j)^*\\varphi_{\\alpha(i) \\alpha(j)}\n\\right)\n$$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{U}'$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{U}'$", "MATH_0013": "$\\beta : I' \\to I$", "MATH_0014": "$h : X' \\to X$", "MATH_0015": "$h'_i : X'_i \\to X_{\\beta(i)}$", "MATH_0016": "$g = h$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-definition-morphism-coverings}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{remark-easier-family}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-family-is-one}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-pullback}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-pullback-family}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9f101f35975b1ef913b8416e3086ddb31576003a652727e98316829bebe4059e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6acaefab5cb306d0853c45803fb4372bc3c0a0a194c364db8ca3cada51cd6753", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> and\n<MATH_0003> be families of morphisms with\nfixed target. Let <MATH_0004>, <MATH_0005> and\n<MATH_0006> be a morphism of families\nof maps with fixed target, see\nSites, Definition <REF_0001>.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> Let <MATH_0007> be a descent datum relative to the\nfamily <MATH_0008>. The system\n<MATH_0009>\n(with notation as in Remark <REF_0002>)\nis a descent datum relative to <MATH_0010>.\n<STRUCT_0003> This construction defines a functor between the category of\ndescent data relative to <MATH_0011> and the category of\ndescent data relative to <MATH_0012>.\n<STRUCT_0004> Given a second <MATH_0013>, <MATH_0014> and\n<MATH_0015> morphism of families\nof maps with fixed target, then if <MATH_0016> the two resulting functors\nbetween descent data are canonically isomorphic.\n<STRUCT_0005> These functors agree, via Lemma <REF_0003>,\nwith the pullback functors constructed in Lemma <REF_0004>.\n<STRUCT_0006>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bdcfe6c2a57253d78da0068cc32f2a9f5d99e5aadaab7c412a6a8cfdd54751b5", "unit_id": "tag:0ADN:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0ADF", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-pullback}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-family-is-one}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:067c419260b967aeaf32cc916cd4ef8f46c71719123e6f978d1882a9ff9fda86", "source_text": "This follows from Lemma <REF_0001> via the\ncorrespondence of Lemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fd5bc09f89dbec30b1da9ea91b19be522d5e8feb95d7f2c9f0832fe2f51e4e86", "unit_id": "tag:0ADN:proof"}
{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0ADF", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{U}' = \\{X'_i \\to X'\\}_{i \\in I'}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{U} = \\{X_i \\to X\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\alpha : I' \\to I$", "MATH_0004": "$g : X' \\to X$", "MATH_0005": "$g_i : X'_i \\to X_{\\alpha(i)}$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n(V_i, \\varphi_{ij}) \\longmapsto\n(g_i^*V_{\\alpha(i)}, (g_i \\times g_j)^*\\varphi_{\\alpha(i) \\alpha(j)})\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-pullback-family}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-pullback-functor-family}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d8decb7fc9e1ab44fd15b9bd30b3d5f567f0b361c04ef5db2d39efffe23ae6bb", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:10ce2eca617d520a2729727627d5c6dd49c71fda7c059ce0850fc23436010438", "source_text": "With <MATH_0001>,\n<MATH_0002>, <MATH_0003>,\n<MATH_0004>, and <MATH_0005> as in\nLemma <REF_0001> the functor\n<MATH_0006>\nconstructed in that lemma\nis called the <TEXTITOPEN_0001>pullback functor<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> on descent data.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0d2371fe5027db67798c38fd1c0d46836716bfacf5398bf5e14eca5967587a64", "unit_id": "tag:0ADP:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0ADF", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{U}'$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{U}'$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0006": "$(\\alpha, g_i)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-definition-morphism-coverings}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-pullback-family}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d5413d830c2ab1864c15606c9656af07bbd7a1526e086a237c75f490f1347b28", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ab75cda42a850fe8be4f4eac30fae9a70517702dcf3ca7d2ae47b89946794cb2", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIf <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> have the same target <MATH_0003>,\nand if <MATH_0004> refines <MATH_0005> (see\nSites, Definition <REF_0001>)\nbut no explicit pair <MATH_0006> is given, then we can still\ntalk about the pullback functor since we have seen in\nLemma <REF_0002> that the choice of the pair does not matter\n(up to a canonical isomorphism).\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e13d62be26629e49602c739cfd065bab66c65355b77b9915d69afd39ac5a667b", "unit_id": "tag:0ADF:prose-0004"}
